To create a React hook for converting between different temperature units, follow these steps:

1. Create a new file named `useTemperatureConverter.js` in your React project.
2. Export a function called `useTemperatureConverter`:
```javascript
export default function useTemperatureConverter() {
  const [temperature, setTemperature] = React.useState(0);
  const [unit, setUnit] = React.useState('celsius');

  const handleConvert = (newUnit) => {
    if (newUnit === 'celsius') {
      setTemperature((prevTemperature) => Math.round(prevTemperature * 9 / 5) + 32);
      setUnit('fahrenheit');
    } else {
      setTemperature((prevTemperature) => Math.round(prevTemperature - 32) * 5 / 9);
      setUnit('celsius');
    }
  };

  return { temperature, unit, handleConvert };
}
```
1. In your component, import the `useTemperatureConverter` hook and use it:
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { useTemperatureConverter } from './useTemperatureConverter';

const TemperatureConverter = () => {
  const { temperature, unit, handleConvert } = useTemperatureConverter();

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Temperature Converter</h2>
      <p>Current temperature: {temperature} {unit}</p>
      <button onClick={() => handleConvert('fahrenheit')}>Convert to Fahrenheit</button>
      <button onClick={() => handleConvert('celsius')}>Convert to Celsius</button>
    </div>
  );
};

export default TemperatureConverter;
```
This hook allows you to easily convert between Celsius and Fahrenheit temperatures in your React components. You can use the `handleConvert` function to switch between the two units.

