Yes, you can upload images to MongoDB using the `GridFS` (Grid File System) feature. GridFS allows you to store large files, such as images, as a collection of chunks in MongoDB. This helps to optimize storage and improve query performance.

To upload an image to MongoDB using GridFS, follow these steps:

1. Install the `mongoose` library for Node.js if you haven't already.
