5. Use the `gridfs` package to upload the image data to MongoDB. You can use the `gridfs.createReadStream()` method to create a readable stream from the image file, and then pipe that stream to the `gridfs.upload()` method to upload the image to MongoDB.
6. Once the upload is complete, you can retrieve the uploaded image from MongoDB using the `gridfs.findOne()` method and the `_id` of the uploaded document.

